FLAKINESS
  The concurrency test was run 8x consecutively against the fixture and passed 8/8.
  Its `netIncome` is deliberately NOT pinned to a literal: depending on where the
  loser's balance read falls relative to the winner's COMMIT it is legitimately
  either 700 or 0, and pinning either would be asserting a race. The RESIDUAL is
  pinned, because it is re-read after the journal exists and is 0 under both
  interleavings. An earlier draft that pinned netIncome failed ~40% of runs; the
  first draft of the fix itself (residual from the stale read) failed 3 of 6.

NOT DONE
  Migration 627 deliberately NOT renumbered — see fix.md, it is a merge-time action.
